      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Platform & dependencies: the principal view\nWhat this system is made of, where its limits are, and what will break first.\nRead it when a symptom on **Service health** needs a *cause*, or before a capacity decision.\n\n**Dependencies** (row 1) are things SaucerJam needs but does not control: Cloudflare, the Postgres behind Supabase, Fider, and the Oracle host.\n**Data plane** (row 2) is the database; **capacity** (rows 3-4) is how full each layer is; **change correlation** (row 5) ties errors to deploys.\n\n**Rule of thumb (Google SRE):** saturation is a *leading* indicator \u2014 act before 100%, because latency degrades first and players feel it before a graph turns red."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Dependency health: can we reach the things we depend on?",
